	<body>
		<div class="container">
			<nav class="breadcrumb">
				<a href="/">Home</a>
				<span>/</span>
				<a href="/guides">Guides</a>
				<span>/</span>
				<span>Presearch</span>
			</nav>

			<h1>Presearch Search Engine</h1>
			<p class="intro">Decentralized search with crypto rewards and no tracking.</p>

			<nav class="toc">
				<h2>Contents</h2>
				<ol>
					<li><a href="#what-is">What is Presearch?</a></li>
					<li><a href="#how-it-works">How It Works</a></li>
					<li><a href="#rewards">PRE Token Rewards</a></li>
					<li><a href="#privacy">Privacy Features</a></li>
					<li><a href="#search-quality">Search Quality</a></li>
					<li><a href="#pros-cons">Pros and Cons</a></li>
					<li><a href="#setup">How to Use Presearch</a></li>
					<li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
				</ol>
			</nav>

			<section id="what-is">
				<h2>What is Presearch?</h2>
				<p>Presearch is a decentralized, open-source search engine that aims to challenge Google's dominance. Unlike traditional search engines, Presearch:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Runs on a decentralized network of nodes</li>
					<li>Rewards users with PRE cryptocurrency for searching</li>
					<li>Doesn't track users or build profiles</li>
					<li>Aggregates results from multiple search sources</li>
					<li>Is community-driven and open source</li>
				</ul>

				<div class="highlight-box">
					<h3>Quick Facts</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Launched:</strong> 2017</li>
						<li><strong>Index:</strong> Multiple sources (aggregated)</li>
						<li><strong>AI Features:</strong> None</li>
						<li><strong>Tracking:</strong> None</li>
						<li><strong>Unique:</strong> Earn PRE crypto tokens</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="how-it-works">
				<h2>How Presearch Works</h2>

				<h3>Decentralized Architecture</h3>
				<p>Unlike Google's centralized servers, Presearch runs on a network of community-operated nodes:</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Node operators</strong> - Community members run nodes and earn PRE tokens</li>
					<li><strong>No single point of control</strong> - Distributed infrastructure</li>
					<li><strong>Censorship resistant</strong> - Harder to manipulate or shut down</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Search Sources</h3>
				<p>Presearch aggregates results from multiple search providers:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Google (optional)</li>
					<li>Bing</li>
					<li>DuckDuckGo</li>
					<li>Wikipedia</li>
					<li>And many others via "providers"</li>
				</ul>
				<p>You can customize which providers appear in your results.</p>

				<h3>Keyword Staking</h3>
				<p>Advertisers stake PRE tokens on keywords. When someone searches that keyword, staked ads appear. This creates a transparent, decentralized advertising model without tracking.</p>
			</section>

			<section id="rewards">
				<h2>PRE Token Rewards</h2>

				<div class="method-box">
					<h3>How to Earn PRE</h3>
					<ol>
						<li>Create a free Presearch account</li>
						<li>Set Presearch as your default search engine</li>
						<li>Search as you normally would</li>
						<li>Earn up to 0.1 PRE per search (max ~25/day)</li>
						<li>Withdraw at 1,000 PRE or stake for advertising</li>
					</ol>
				</div>

				<h3>Reward Details</h3>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Rate:</strong> ~0.1 PRE per qualifying search</li>
					<li><strong>Daily cap:</strong> Approximately 25 searches rewarded per day</li>
					<li><strong>Minimum withdrawal:</strong> 1,000 PRE</li>
					<li><strong>Token value:</strong> Varies (check exchanges for current price)</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>What to Do with PRE</h3>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Withdraw:</strong> Transfer to a crypto wallet and sell</li>
					<li><strong>Stake on keywords:</strong> Advertise your own content</li>
					<li><strong>Run a node:</strong> Stake PRE to operate a search node</li>
					<li><strong>Hold:</strong> Keep tokens hoping value increases</li>
				</ul>

				<div class="warning">
					<strong>Note:</strong> Cryptocurrency values are volatile. PRE token value can go up or down. Don't rely on Presearch rewards as income.
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="privacy">
				<h2>Privacy Features</h2>

				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag green">No Tracking</span>
							<span class="engine-tag">Decentralized</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<h3>What Presearch Doesn't Collect</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>Search history linked to identity (without account)</li>
						<li>User behavior profiles</li>
						<li>Cross-site tracking data</li>
						<li>Personal information for advertising</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>With an Account</h3>
					<p>If you create an account to earn rewards:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Email address is stored</li>
						<li>Search count is tracked (for rewards)</li>
						<li>Searches are not linked to your account for profiling</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>Anonymous Use</h3>
					<p>You can use Presearch without an account for full anonymity - you just won't earn rewards.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="search-quality">
				<h2>Search Quality</h2>

				<h3>Strengths</h3>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Multiple sources</strong> - Aggregates from several search engines</li>
					<li><strong>Customizable</strong> - Choose which providers to include</li>
					<li><strong>No filter bubbles</strong> - Same results for everyone</li>
					<li><strong>Instant answers</strong> - Wikipedia, calculations, etc.</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Weaknesses</h3>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Less polished</strong> - Interface not as refined as Google</li>
					<li><strong>Variable quality</strong> - Depends on which providers are enabled</li>
					<li><strong>Slower</strong> - Aggregation can add latency</li>
					<li><strong>Limited features</strong> - Fewer advanced search tools</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Best Use Cases</h3>
				<p>Presearch works well for:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>General web searches</li>
					<li>Users who want decentralization</li>
					<li>Those interested in earning crypto</li>
					<li>Privacy-focused searches</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section id="pros-cons">
				<h2>Pros and Cons</h2>

				<div class="pros-cons">
					<div class="pros">
						<h4>Pros</h4>
						<ul>
							<li>Earn crypto for searching</li>
							<li>Decentralized infrastructure</li>
							<li>No tracking or profiles</li>
							<li>Open source</li>
							<li>Multiple search providers</li>
							<li>Community-driven</li>
							<li>No AI features</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="cons">
						<h4>Cons</h4>
						<ul>
							<li>Results less polished</li>
							<li>Slower than centralized options</li>
							<li>Crypto rewards are small</li>
							<li>1,000 PRE withdrawal minimum</li>
							<li>Less comprehensive results</li>
							<li>Learning curve for features</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="setup">
				<h2>How to Use Presearch</h2>

				<div class="browser-section">
					<h3>Quick Start (No Account)</h3>
					<p>Just visit <code>presearch.com</code> and search. No signup required for basic use.</p>

					<h3>To Earn Rewards</h3>
					<ol>
						<li>Go to <code>presearch.com</code></li>
						<li>Click "Sign Up" and create an account</li>
						<li>Verify your email</li>
						<li>Start searching to earn PRE</li>
						<li>Check your balance in account settings</li>
					</ol>

					<h3>Set as Default Search Engine</h3>
					<p>Use this URL:</p>
					<code class="code-block">https://presearch.com/search?q=%s</code>

					<a href="/guides/set-default-search-engine" class="cta-button secondary">Full Setup Guide</a>
				</div>

				<div class="browser-section" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
					<h3>Browser Extension</h3>
					<p>Presearch offers a browser extension that:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Sets Presearch as your default search</li>
						<li>Keeps you logged in for rewards</li>
						<li>Available for Chrome, Firefox, and Edge</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="faq">
				<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>What is Presearch?</h3>
					<p>Presearch is a decentralized search engine that doesn't track users and rewards them with PRE cryptocurrency tokens. It aggregates results from multiple sources and runs on community-operated nodes.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>How do Presearch rewards work?</h3>
					<p>Create a free account, search normally, and earn ~0.1 PRE per search (up to ~25 per day). Once you reach 1,000 PRE, you can withdraw to a crypto wallet or stake tokens for advertising.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Is Presearch private?</h3>
					<p>Yes. Presearch doesn't track your searches or build profiles. Without an account, it's fully anonymous. With an account, only your email and search count (for rewards) are stored - searches aren't linked to your identity.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Is Presearch better than Google?</h3>
					<p>For privacy and earning rewards, yes. For search quality, Google is still better for complex queries. Presearch is best for users who value decentralization and don't mind slightly less polished results.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>How much can I earn with Presearch?</h3>
					<p>You can earn approximately 25 PRE per day (maximum). The actual dollar value depends on PRE's market price, which fluctuates. Don't expect to earn significant money - think of it as a bonus for using a privacy-focused search engine.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<div class="next-steps">
				<h2>Next Steps</h2>
				<div class="next-links">
					<a href="/guides/best-private-search-engines">
						<span>Compare</span>
						<strong>Best Private Search Engines</strong>
					</a>
					<a href="/guides/set-default-search-engine">
						<span>Setup</span>
						<strong>Set as Default Search</strong>
					</a>
					<a href="/guides/mojeek-search-engine">
						<span>Alternative</span>
						<strong>Mojeek Search</strong>
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</body>
</html>

